WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.476 --> 00:00:04.061
- A horse knows what
they're supposed to do

00:00:04.061 --> 00:00:06.478
by what your legs are asking.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:08.705
The way you sit in that saddle,

00:00:08.705 --> 00:00:11.288
the way your legs move, the
way your calves tighten,

00:00:11.288 --> 00:00:12.820
the way your feet bump a horse,

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:16.547
all of those things are communication.

00:00:16.547 --> 00:00:19.757
I guess you could say
I'm at a disadvantage.

00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:21.182
I can only use my hands and my voice

00:00:21.182 --> 00:00:25.349
to communicate with my horse
because I can't move my legs.

00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:29.689
(horse neighing)

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.707
My name is Amberley Snyder,

00:00:35.707 --> 00:00:38.707
and I'm a professional barrel racer.

00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:43.831
Barrel racing is a speed
event in the world of rodeo.

00:00:43.831 --> 00:00:45.839
There are three barrels
set up in the arena

00:00:45.839 --> 00:00:48.890
and you do a cloverleaf
pattern around those barrels

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:52.640
and it's all timed, so
the fastest time wins.

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:56.029
Barrel racing isn't just what I do;

00:00:56.029 --> 00:01:00.117
my horses and competing in
rodeo, it's a part of who I am.

00:01:00.117 --> 00:01:03.167
I started riding at three and competing

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:06.484
in barrel racing at the age of seven.

00:01:06.484 --> 00:01:08.107
Just have loved it ever since then,

00:01:08.107 --> 00:01:10.410
I mean I've done it all
through junior rodeo days,

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.079
up into high school, college rodeo,

00:01:12.079 --> 00:01:15.079
and now into the professional level.

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:23.271
Only days before I was going
to buy my pro rodeo permit,

00:01:23.271 --> 00:01:25.140
I was in a rollover car accident

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.488
where I was ejected and broke my back,

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:31.738
which paralyzed me from the waist down.

00:01:34.042 --> 00:01:36.145
Doctors told me slim to no chance

00:01:36.145 --> 00:01:37.501
that I would be able to walk again.

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:40.111
It was going to be impossible to ride.

00:01:40.111 --> 00:01:41.893
That wasn't an option for me,

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:43.288
riding was what I was going to do,

00:01:43.288 --> 00:01:46.699
I didn't care what had to happen.

00:01:46.699 --> 00:01:48.407
After I started doing therapy,

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:50.978
sensation started coming back in my legs.

00:01:50.978 --> 00:01:55.684
When I got back on my
horses, that only got better.

00:01:55.684 --> 00:01:57.074
The very first time I
got back on my horse,

00:01:57.074 --> 00:02:01.604
I realized that it wasn't
going to be the same.

00:02:01.604 --> 00:02:04.104
The biggest change is balance.

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:07.935
I went through modifications,
seatbelt on my saddle,

00:02:07.935 --> 00:02:09.205
Velcro straps around my legs,

00:02:09.205 --> 00:02:13.231
all these pieces that made
it so that I could ride.

00:02:13.231 --> 00:02:17.218
The horse I have now, his
name is Legacy, aka Legs.

00:02:17.218 --> 00:02:19.211
I named him that because
that's what he becomes

00:02:19.211 --> 00:02:22.827
every time I get to leave
my wheelchair in my trailer.

00:02:22.827 --> 00:02:25.392
I now have to use my hands and my voice

00:02:25.392 --> 00:02:29.811
where my legs were now
a piece I couldn't use.

00:02:29.811 --> 00:02:31.590
He's the one that has made all of

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:33.612
those impossible things possible.

00:02:33.612 --> 00:02:35.149
I mean he is the one that
has brought me back into

00:02:35.149 --> 00:02:40.038
that arena to be not just a
participant but a competitor.

00:02:40.038 --> 00:02:42.153
To make the national finals rodeo

00:02:42.153 --> 00:02:46.770
and be a world champion barrel
racer is my biggest goal.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:50.771
I've won over 70 buckles
before my accident

00:02:50.771 --> 00:02:53.042
but this buckle, this is my first buckle

00:02:53.042 --> 00:02:54.773
I won since my accident.

00:02:54.773 --> 00:02:58.190
Took me six years to get to win this one.

00:02:59.606 --> 00:03:02.006
There's been points
where I wanted to quit,

00:03:02.006 --> 00:03:06.259
there's been points
where it's been too hard.

00:03:06.259 --> 00:03:07.712
It doesn't matter what the odds are,

00:03:07.712 --> 00:03:09.494
it doesn't matter what people say,

00:03:09.494 --> 00:03:10.458
you're the only one that gets

00:03:10.458 --> 00:03:13.175
to decide what you're capable of.

00:03:13.175 --> 00:03:16.592
(uplifting guitar music)

